local

# Build artifacts
build/

# Root-level compiled binaries. `go build ./cmd/x` and `go build ./samples/x`
# drop their output here, and four of them were committed by accident. That is
# not merely untidy: publish-oss.sh rsyncs the WORKING TREE, so anything tracked
# at root ships to the public repo verbatim. Three of these were live on
# AI-AgentLens/agentshield-oss for months with 19 embedded build paths of the
# form /Users/<handle>/dev/<old-private-repo-name>/... — the privacy scan in
# publish-oss.sh reads text files and cannot see inside a Mach-O.
# Build to ./build/ or use `go run`; never commit a binary at root.
/cli-demo
/mcp-demo
/server
/gen-premium-manifest

